@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
' purpose: a forfeit is a loss — not a draw, not an abandoned row, not a missing result
' status: proposed 2026-09-17, not implemented; _spec/_plans/ is exempt from the SPEC-reference rule.
' would touch: not in this tree — no forfeit, result, or rating types exist under
'   the sandbox checkout (measured 2026-09-17). Locate the owning engine
'   module before a covers: line can be honest.
'   draw handling that must stay distinct _spec/_plans/turn-45-draw-stop.puml
'   analytics that will ingest the result .. _spec/_plans/chess-analytics.puml
'   the journey that offers the verb ....... _spec/_plans/chess-user-journey.puml
' Notes are capped at 5 lines x 50 columns; one idea per anchor.
'
' ── WHAT THE LINE ITEM SETTLES ─────────────────────────────────────────────
' "treat forfeit as loss" is an OUTCOME mapping. The player who forfeits loses;
' the opponent wins. Anything else — draw, void, "abandoned", no row — is the
' bug this plan exists to close.
'
' ── WHAT IT DOES NOT SETTLE ────────────────────────────────────────────────
'   who may forfeit (player, both, a disconnected client)
'   whether a timeout is a forfeit or a separate loss reason
'   whether ratings, replays, and export write the same enum
'   copy on the surface: "resign", "quit", "forfeit" may be one verb or three
'
' Mixing this with the turn-45 draw stop would hide a draw bug inside a forfeit
' patch. They share an outcome table and nothing else.
title PLANNED — a forfeit writes a loss;\nit is not a draw and not a void

component "the player concedes" as QUIT <<app>>
component "outcome table" as OUT <<app>>
component "**draw / void / missing row**\nwhat a forfeit must not become" as WRONG <<error>>
component "loss for the conceding side\nwin for the opponent" as LOSS <<app>>
component "ratings · replay · export" as SINK <<app>>
component "analytics tallies" as AN <<app>>

QUIT ARROW_MAIN OUT
OUT ARROW_ERROR WRONG : today, if the mapping is loose
OUT ARROW_OPTIONAL LOSS : what this plan requires
LOSS ARROW_MAIN SINK
LOSS ARROW_MAIN AN

note bottom of WRONG
  **A missing outcome record is still defective
  because ratings and export cannot recover an
  unwritten loss.** Mapping forfeit onto loss has
  to land together with the persistence write.
end note

note bottom of LOSS
  **Forfeit remains a recorded reason while loss
  is the result every consumer must observe.**
  Preserve the reason for replay, but every query
  that asks who won has to report a loss.
end note

note right of AN
  **Analytics cannot lead this mapping because
  tallies that ingest a void will lie after
  concede becomes a loss.** The dashboard waits on
  this enumeration rather than inventing a second
  scorer.
end note

legend bottom
  **The order to do it in**
  ==
  **1. Print the outcome enum.** Find every writer of a finished game: live
  play, timeout, disconnect, tutorial exit. Name what a forfeit writes today.
  --
  **2. Map forfeit → loss in one place.** One function, one test table: conceding
  side loses, opponent wins, reason remains forfeit. Do not special-case
  tutorials or replays unless a test names them.
  ==
  **3. Point every sink at that function.** Ratings, localStorage export, and
  analytics must not re-derive the winner. The turn-45 draw path stays a
  draw resolver — do not fold it into this mapping.
  --
  **Left open**: timeout vs forfeit; whether "resign" is the same verb; ranked
  vs unranked.
end legend
@enduml
